  <p class="has-text-align-center"><a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/">Contact Dolphin Centrifuge Today</a></p>

  <h3 id="system-specifications">System Specifications</h3>

  <p>To find a more efficient solution, the facility partnered with Dolphin Centrifuge, an independent remanufacturer and system builder of Alfa Laval waste oil centrifuges. Dolphin Centrifuge recommended installing the DMPX-028 disc stack, a self-cleaning centrifuge. This is a purpose-modified <a href="/alfa-laval-centrifuge/">Alfa Laval centrifuge</a> for high-efficiency waste oil processing.</p>

  <p>This is a single-stage train - basic pre-straining removes large debris (nuts, bolts, rocks), then a self-cleaning disc-stack centrifuge (DMPX-028, based on the Alfa Laval MOPX 207) removes the main used-motor-oil contaminants: fine metal particles, ash, water, and glycol/antifreeze.</p>

  <p>Each DMPX-028 unit processes up to 20 gallons per minute (GPM) at 180°F. By deploying one unit operating continuously for 16 hours a day over 250 days a year, a total processing capacity of 4,800,000 gallons annually was achieved.</p>

